,"Diminutive of Scherf, from Middle High German scherf, scherpf (“a coin of small value, esp. a halfpenny”), from Old High German scerf, ultimately from Proto-Germanic *skrapōną (“to scratch”).\nRelated to modern Scherbe (“shard”) and Middle High German scharben (“to notch, to nick”) (from Old High German scarbōn, cognate with Old English sceorfan (“to gnaw, to bite”)), because the coins were originally notched so they could be broken up for payment when needed.\nIntroduced by Luther as a translation for the Ancient Greek λεπτόν (leptón, “small coin”) in Mark 12:42.",{"g":"n","decl":"|||s||||"}]],"senses":[[600763,"scherflein","noun","widow's mite, i.e. a small donation or contribution, esp. of monetary kind.",0,"n"]]},"unbekleideten":{"entries":[["unbekleideten",null,null,null]],"senses":[[564596,"unbekleideten","adj","inflection of unbekleidet:",0],[564597,"unbekleideten","adj","strong genitive masculine/neuter singular",1],[564598,"unbekleideten","adj","weak/mixed genitive/dative all-gender singular",2],[564599,"unbekleideten","adj","strong/weak/mixed accusative masculine singular",3],[564600,"unbekleideten","adj","strong dative plural",4],[564601,"unbekleideten","adj","weak/mixed all-case plural",5]],"inflections":[["unbekleideten","unbekleidet","genitive,masculine,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"aufwirblet":{"inflections":[["aufwirblet","aufwirbeln","plural,second-person,subjunctive,subjunctive-i,subordinate-clause"]]},"barbäuchige":{"inflections":[["barbäuchige","barbäuchig","feminine,nominative,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"davonrenntest":{"inflections":[["davonrenntest","davonrennen","formal,rare,second-person,singular,subjunctive,subjunctive-ii,subordinate-clause"]]},"pfalzens":{"inflections":[["pfalzens","pfalzen","genitive"]]},"unzukömmlicher":{"inflections":[["unzukömmlicher","unzukömmlich","masculine,nominative,singular,strong"]]}}}